# The properness criterion of Proposition 11 and of step 4 of Theorem 15

For an embedding problem with abelian kernel in the abstract setting `Work.Properness.Setup`, a
*lift* (solution) `ψ : H →* E` of `ρ` is **proper** if it is surjective.  Because `π ∘ ψ = ρ` is
surjective, this happens if and only if `ψ(H_K) = A`, where `H_K = ker ρ` is the subgroup cut out
by the intermediate field `K` of the paper.

The content of the paper's properness argument (Proposition 11, and step 4 of Theorem 15) is
purely of this shape:

> if `S i ≤ H_K` is a family of subgroups (the decomposition groups of primes that split
> completely in `K`) and the images `ψ(S i)` generate `A`, then `ψ(H_K) = A`, so `ψ` is proper.

This file records that criterion in the several equivalent forms used in the paper.

## Main declarations (clean API; see also the raw lemmas below)

* `Work.Properness.Setup.isProper_iff_map_HK_eq_A` — `ψ` proper `↔ ψ(H_K) = A`;
* `Work.Properness.Setup.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq` — the criterion: a family `S i ≤ H_K` whose
  images generate `A` forces properness;
* `Work.Properness.iSup_map_le_map_HK` — the paper's first observation
  `⟨⋃ i, ψ(S i)⟩ ≤ ψ(H_K)` for `S i ≤ H_K`;
* `Work.Properness.isProper_of_closure_iUnion_map_eq`,
  `Work.Properness.isProper_of_closure_range_eq` — the same in the "subgroup generated by a union"
  and "subgroup generated by a family of elements" forms in which the paper states it;
* `Work.Properness.isProper_iff_range_eq_top` — properness as `ψ(H) = E`.

## Implementation note

The lemmas `Work.Properness.isProper_iff_map_HK_eq_A` and
`Work.Properness.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq` (without the `Setup.` prefix) are the "raw" versions
proved by the library's lemma agents; their statements carry dummy `{u v w : Universe}` binders,
which makes them awkward to apply.  `Setup.isProper_iff_map_HK_eq_A` and
`Setup.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq` above are the same statements with a clean universe interface, and
are what callers should use.  See `Submission/Work/Properness/NOTES.md`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.Properness.Defs
import Submission.Work.Properness.isProper_iff_map_HK_eq_A
import Submission.Work.Properness.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq
-- PORT435-BEGIN (v4.35 isDefEq respectTransparency compat)
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
-- PORT435-END

namespace Work.Properness

open scoped Classical

noncomputable section

universe u₀ v₀ w₀ ι₀

/-- Properness of a lift is the statement that its range is all of `E` (a formal unfolding of
`Setup.IsProper`). -/
theorem isProper_iff_range_eq_top {S : Setup.{u₀, v₀, w₀}} (ψ : S.Lift) :
    S.IsProper ψ ↔ ψ.1.range = ⊤ :=
  MonoidHom.range_eq_top.symm

/-- **The paper's first observation.**  If `S i ≤ H_K` for all `i`, then the images `ψ(S i)` are
contained in `ψ(H_K)`: `⟨⋃ i, ψ(S i)⟩ ≤ ψ(H_K)`. -/
theorem iSup_map_le_map_HK {S : Setup.{u₀, v₀, w₀}} {ι : Type ι₀} (ψ : S.Lift)
    (T : ι → Subgroup S.H) (hT : ∀ i, T i ≤ S.HK) :
    (⨆ i, (T i).map ψ.1) ≤ S.HK.map ψ.1 :=
  iSup_le fun i => Subgroup.map_mono (hT i)

/-- **The properness criterion of Proposition 11: `ψ` is proper if and only if `ψ(H_K) = A`.**

A proper solution of the embedding problem is a surjection `ψ` with `π ∘ ψ = ρ`; since `ρ` is
surjective, this happens exactly when `ψ(H_K) = A`, where `H_K = ker ρ` is the subgroup fixing the
field cut out by `ρ` (the paper's `G_K`). -/
theorem Setup.isProper_iff_map_HK_eq_A {S : Setup.{u₀, v₀, w₀}} (ψ : S.Lift) :
    S.IsProper ψ ↔ S.HK.map ψ.1 = S.A :=
  @Work.Properness.isProper_iff_map_HK_eq_A.{w₀, v₀, u₀, 0} PUnit PUnit.unit PUnit.unit PUnit.unit
    S ψ

/-- **The properness criterion of Proposition 11, step 4 of Theorem 15.**  If `T i ≤ H_K` is a
family of subgroups whose images under a lift `ψ` generate the abelian kernel `A`, then `ψ` is
proper.  In the paper the `T i` are the decomposition groups of primes that split completely in
the field `K` cut out by `ρ`, and the `φ i : T i →* A` that generate `A` are prescribed by the
Grunwald–Wang local conditions. -/
theorem Setup.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq {S : Setup.{u₀, v₀, w₀}} {ι : Type ι₀} (ψ : S.Lift)
    (T : ι → Subgroup S.H) (hT : ∀ i, T i ≤ S.HK)
    (hgen : (⨆ i, (T i).map ψ.1) = S.A) : S.IsProper ψ :=
  @Work.Properness.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq.{w₀, v₀, u₀, ι₀, 0} PUnit PUnit.unit PUnit.unit
    PUnit.unit S ι ψ T hT hgen

/-- **The properness criterion, in the "subgroup generated by a union" form.**  If a family
`S i ≤ H_K` has images whose union generates the abelian kernel `A`, then every lift of `ρ` is
surjective.  This is the form in which the criterion is used in Proposition 11
(`⟨⋃ i, ψ(G_{k_{p_i}})⟩ = A`). -/
theorem isProper_of_closure_iUnion_map_eq {S : Setup.{u₀, v₀, w₀}} {ι : Type ι₀} (ψ : S.Lift)
    (T : ι → Subgroup S.H) (hT : ∀ i, T i ≤ S.HK)
    (hgen : Subgroup.closure (⋃ i, ((T i).map ψ.1 : Set S.E)) = S.A) : S.IsProper ψ := by
  refine S.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq ψ T hT ?_
  rw [← hgen, Subgroup.closure_iUnion]
  exact iSup_congr fun i => (Subgroup.closure_eq (K := (T i).map ψ.1)).symm

/-- **The properness criterion, in the "generating family of elements" form.**  If elements `φ i`
lie in the images `ψ(S i)` of subgroups `S i ≤ H_K` and generate the abelian kernel `A`, then `ψ`
is proper. -/
theorem isProper_of_closure_range_eq {S : Setup.{u₀, v₀, w₀}} {ι : Type ι₀} (ψ : S.Lift)
    (T : ι → Subgroup S.H) (hT : ∀ i, T i ≤ S.HK) (φ : ι → S.E)
    (hφ : ∀ i, φ i ∈ (T i).map ψ.1) (hgen : Subgroup.closure (Set.range φ) = S.A) :
    S.IsProper ψ := by
  have h1 : Subgroup.closure (Set.range φ) ≤ ⨆ i, (T i).map ψ.1 := by
    rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
    rintro x ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact le_iSup (fun j => (T j).map ψ.1) i (hφ i)
  have h2 : (⨆ i, (T i).map ψ.1) ≤ S.A :=
    iSup_le fun i => le_trans (Subgroup.map_mono (hT i)) (S.map_HK_le_A ψ)
  rw [hgen] at h1
  exact S.isProper_of_iSup_map_eq ψ T hT (le_antisymm h2 h1)

end

end Work.Properness
